{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 280,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Have you ever noticed that some rounded stones\nare almost spherical, while others are kind"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4240,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of flat like a bar of soap?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6130,
    "dDurationMs": 3259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The spherical stones form that way because\nthey never have the chance to settle into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9389,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a preferred orientation: they're either sloshing\naround in pot holes, or rolling along the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13999,
    "dDurationMs": 4001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bottom of a river, or if they're small enough,\ngetting blown around by the wind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18000,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since they have no preferred orientation,\nthese stones get weathered the same amount"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21660,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on all sides, and they'll end up looking the\nsame from all sides as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25300,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's spherical symmetry!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26920,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for flat stones, even if they're a smooth\ndisk perfect for skipping, there's obviously"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31420,
    "dDurationMs": 4829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a preferred, or special, orientation - the\ndirection perpendicular to, or 'away from'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36249,
    "dDurationMs": 1191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the flat sides."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37440,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where did this preference come from?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38920,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And how do flat stones get flat?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40950,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41950,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's kind of like the difference between dumplings\nand biscuits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44890,
    "dDurationMs": 3929,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A dumpling is a lump of dough dropped in a\npot of water, and gravity doesn't really affect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48819,
    "dDurationMs": 3141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its orientation very much when it's rolling\nand bobbing about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51960,
    "dDurationMs": 4559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A biscuit, on the other hand, is a lump of\ndough pulled down by gravity onto a baking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56519,
    "dDurationMs": 4031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sheet, so it tends to be flat and has a clear\ntop and bottom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60550,
    "dDurationMs": 4169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And while the details are ultimately more\ncomplicated, when sedimentary rock forms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64719,
    "dDurationMs": 4351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it forms layers, or when stones too heavy\nto roll are worn down by abrasion at the bottom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69070,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of a river or lake, they tend to be worn a\nbit flat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71490,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In both cases the preferred direction is dictated\nby gravity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75820,
    "dDurationMs": 3909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And gravity is also why we build buildings\nin layers, with a basement, floors and a roof"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79729,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– if we were in outer space without a preferred\ndirection from gravity, we'd probably just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84079,
    "dDurationMs": 851,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "live in blobs."
    } ]
  } ]
}
